course: dictionary
lesson: 3988
title: Ships from long ago
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a time long ago, and the words around them can give you clues. Read the whole sentence. «Manila galleons crossed the Pacific between Acapulco and Manila» tells you a galleon is something that sails across an ocean.
explain: The next clue is «carrying American silver one way and Chinese silk and porcelain the other.» Ships carry cargo, so a galleon must be a big ship that carried valuable goods. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "Manila ships crossed the Pacific carrying silver" still makes sense, so your guess fits.
explain: The dictionary gives the full picture. A galleon was a large sailing ship with several masts and decks, used long ago by Spain, England and other countries for war and trade.
fact: A galleon was a large sailing ship with several masts and decks.
fact: Galleons were used long ago by Spain, England and other countries for war and trade.
fact: Galleons carried gold, silver and goods across the oceans, so pirates often attacked them.
fact: «Treasure galleon» means a galleon loaded with valuable things such as gold and silver.
fact: Context helps: «Manila galleons crossed the Pacific» shows that a galleon sailed across an ocean.
exercise: What was a galleon? | *A large sailing ship with several masts and decks | A small rowing boat for fishing | A train that crossed the Pacific | A kind of silver coin
exercise: «carrying American silver one way and Chinese silk and porcelain the other» What did galleons carry? | Apples and fish | Gold and silver only | *Valuable goods such as silver, silk and porcelain | Sand and stones
exercise: What does sunken mean in «a sunken galleon»? | Sailing very fast | *Gone down under the sea | Built of wood | Full of treasure
test: Which word in «Manila galleons crossed the Pacific» shows that a galleon sailed over water? | Between | Manila | *Pacific | Until
test: Why might a pirate want to attack a galleon? | Because galleons were made of paper | Because pirates like the colour blue | Because galleons were small and slow | *Because galleons carried gold and silver
exam: A sentence says «Manila galleons crossed the Pacific.» What does a galleon most likely do? | Flies above the clouds | Grows on the seabed | *Sails across the sea carrying goods | Walks across the sea
